  <h3>Wich ways are there to apply visual hierarchy to your design?</h3>
  <p>
    Look what elements are most important and what are important details and
    what background informations is.
  </p>
  <p>Then use:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Color Contrants</li>
    <li>Scale</li>
    <li>White space and position</li>
    <li>Font</li>
    <li>Thickness of font</li>
    <li>Animation</li>
  </ul>
  <p>To Guide the viewer along the page, through the hierarchy.</p>
  <h3>What levels of visual hierarchy did you learn?</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>Important information</li>
    <li>Important details</li>
    <li>Background information</li>
  </ol>
  <h3>Who is Joshua Porter? What does he mean with is quote?</h3>
  <p>
    He was a great user interface designer. His quote was about how important it
    is to guide the viewer along the page with weight.
